cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "Probing the Vacuum: wormhole instability and wormhole-inspired teleportation"
authors:
  - family-names: "Kihara Muchiri"
    given-names: "Gerald"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-17"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  A compact Python reproduction of Shinkai and Hayward's dual-null evolution of the
  Ellis wormhole, linking its collapse-time exponent to the linear unstable mode and
  quantifying the fine-tuning cost of holding the throat open; plus a
  wormhole-inspired teleportation circuit simulated exactly and run on QuTech's
  Tuna-17 processor. Developed with assistance from Claude (Anthropic).
keywords:
  - wormholes
  - numerical relativity
  - dual-null evolution
  - quantum teleportation
  - quantum computing
